# VERIFIED AGAINST THE PAGE IMAGE, 2026-08-02. All 55 cells were read off a
# 200-dpi render of source.pdf p.89 and match this CSV exactly; the caption
# "TABLE 49 / PERFORATION OF 1/8 IN. MILD STEEL" is printed above this table in
# the right half of the page.
#
# Criterion: PERFORATION OF 1/8-IN. MILD STEEL. No energy closure exists --
# 1/2 m v^2 runs 248-930 ft-lb across these rows. Identity was by elimination
# against 105mm-m1-casualties.csv, and is now also direct from the page
# geometry; see 75mm-m48-perforation-1-8in.invariant for the full admissibility
# note and why monotonicity is NOT a column-identity test.
#
# CROSS-SHELL CLOSURE: (m, v) here is identical to 155mm-m107-perforation-1-8in
# on all 11 shared ranges -- both shells fire at 3,500 f/s and (m, v) is a
# single-fragment ballistics result independent of shell size. Checked by
# checks/ordnance-1944-page-geometry.py.
monotonic:  r_ft increasing
monotonic:  N non-increasing
monotonic:  B non-increasing
monotonic:  m_oz non-decreasing
monotonic:  v_fps non-increasing
